# Rust

- Use `cargo test` / `cargo clippy` as documented in the repo; scope to one crate or module when possible.
- Match error types (`thiserror`, `anyhow`, custom enums) already used in the crate.
- Do not add dependencies to `Cargo.toml` without approval.
- Prefer explicit `match` over panics for recoverable errors unless the crate is panic-by-design.
- Keep `unsafe` out unless the codebase already uses it in that layer.
- Follow existing async runtime (tokio/async-std) — do not mix runtimes.
- Run `cargo fmt` expectations only if the repo CI enforces it.
